An addclass bot never opens a trade on its own either.
Touches: modules/mod-playerbots/src/Ai/Base/Actions/TradeAction.cpp,
TradeAction::Execute(); and
modules/mod-playerbots/src/Ai/World/Rpg/Action/RpgSubActions.cpp,
RpgTradeUsefulAction::Execute()

Why: report #118 (recurring after #92/#93). The 0024 gate covered only
IsRandomBot, but the addclass bot family (alt companions) routes through the
same RpgTradeUsefulTrigger -> TradeAction path, and IsAddclassBot passed
straight through it. A companion bot with no master could still open trades
at nearby real players.

Two sites:
- TradeAction keeps its position as the enforcement point (every path into
  CMSG_INITIATE_TRADE goes through it); the gate now refuses both bot kinds.
- RpgTradeUsefulAction returns early before doing any work, so the trigger
  stops selecting an action that can only end in a refusal -- without this
  the AI re-evaluates the same refusal every tick for as long as the
  trigger's friendship roll passes.

Trades the player opens are untouched: TradeStatusAction already handled
completion for both bot kinds, and neither gate reaches it.
